\multicolumn{2}{r}{} & & 0 & 0 & 0 \\
\end{array}
Thus, $x^4-3x^3+15x-25 = (x^2-3x+5)(x^2-4)$.
Therefore, $p(x) = x^2-4$.

We can check this by multiplying $(x^2-3x+5)(x^2-4)$:
\begin{align*} (x^2-3x+5)(x^2-4) &= x^2(x^2-4) - 3x(x^2-4) + 5(x^2-4) \\ &= x^4 - 4x^2 - 3x^3 + 12x + 5x^2 - 20 \\ &= x^4 - 3x^3 + x^2 + 12x - 20 \end{align*}
This is not equal to $x^4-3x^3+15x-25$. Let's recheck the long division.
\begin{array}{c|ccccc}
\multicolumn{2}{r}{x^2} & & -4 \\
\cline{2-6}
x^2-3x+5 & x^4 & -3x^3 & +0x^2 & +15x & -25 \\
\multicolumn{2}{r}{x^4} & -3x^3 & +5x^2 \\
\cline{2-4}
\multicolumn{2}{r}{0} & 0 & -5x^2 & +15x & -25 \\
\multicolumn{2}{r}{} & & -5x^2 & +15x & -25 \\
\cline{4-6}
\multicolumn{2}{r}{} & & 0 & 0 & 0 \\
\end{array}
So we have $x^4-3x^3+15x-25 = (x^2-3x+5)(x^2-5)$.
